    "html": "<p>An ideal gas is heated at a constant pressure of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0 \\times 10^{5}\\text{ Pa}\"></span>. The gas absorbs <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"850\\text{ J}\"></span> of thermal energy, causing its volume to expand from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.5 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}^{3}\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.5 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}^{3}\"></span>. What is the resulting change in the internal energy of the gas?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"450\\text{ J}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"850\\text{ J}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1250\\text{ J}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400\\text{ J}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
